{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 10. h3. White reaches the familiar two-rank formation while Black occupies the center. This quiet illustrative route is not a claim that all ten setup moves are best in every position. Black has more space and can prepare ...e4 or ...d4. White's extra tempo has not prevented a central bind. } 10. h3 Rad8 *

