{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 7. Nd2. Black develops modestly and keeps the center intact. White preserves flexibility while the bishops watch long diagonals. Black may use ...Re8 and ...Bf8 to prepare central expansion. Quiet development can support a serious squeeze. } 7. Nd2 Re8 8. h3 Bd6 9. Ngf3 h6 *

