{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 7. Nd2. Black combines central space with a fianchetto. White's b2 bishop points toward the opposing king side, but central pawns may block its influence. Black can advance ...d4 and restrict the b1 knight. The g7 bishop may become stronger than its white counterpart after exchanges. } 7. Nd2 Qc7 8. Ngf3 Nc6 9. O-O e5 *

