{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 7. Nd2. Black's d6 pawn supports e5 and keeps the center flexible. White can choose a partial Hippo or a more active King's Indian Attack structure. Black can use ...Nc6 and ...Be6 to develop with central influence. A later ...d5 may seize the initiative if White waits too long. } 7. Nd2 a5 8. a4 Nc6 9. e4 Ne8 *

