{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 8. Nbd2. Both sides restrain the center, but the knights on f3 and f6 block the opposing fianchetto diagonals before b-pawn moves expose the corner rooks. This detail prevents a tactical accident. Without a blocker on the long diagonal, b3 or ...b6 can expose a corner rook to the enemy bishop. Never build this formation without tracing the diagonal. } 8. Nbd2 Nbd7 9. b4 c5 10. a3 O-O *

