{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 6. Bb2. Black establishes c5-d5-e5. White must challenge the center before completing every wing pawn move. ...d4 can close the center with a large space advantage. If every white piece lacks squares, the setup has become too slow. } 6. Bb2 Be7 7. Ne2 h5 8. h3 Qc7 *

