{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 5. Ne2. White develops the king knight and prepares king safety against Black's ambitious center. Delaying b3 can be sensible when the center needs urgent attention. Black may push ...e4 or ...f4 with tempo. A slow double fianchetto can become a target if the center opens before White castles. } 5. Ne2 Be6 6. O-O h5 7. c4 dxc4 *

