{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 5. exd4. White exchanges the invading pawn and changes the structure. Black retains a d4 wedge, but White has opened a diagonal and can attack the pawn. The d4 pawn restricts Nc3 and may support a central outpost. Do not place a knight where an enemy pawn can simply capture it. } 5. exd4 exd4 6. Nf3 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 *

