{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 5. dxe4. The central exchange releases Black's knight onto e4. White has prevented a permanent pawn wedge but must now address the active piece. A central knight can threaten forks on c3 or f2 depending on the position. Check its concrete attacks before making another pawn move. } 5. dxe4 Nxe4 6. Nd2 Nxd2 7. Bxd2 c6 *

