{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 7. Bxh3. Black exchanges the g2 bishop and brings the queen toward White's already castled king. White's knight has left g1, so the queen on h3 cannot simply be captured by that knight. If White's knight were still on g1, ...Qxh3 would lose the queen to Nxh3. In this line its different square makes the attack a real concern. } 7. Bxh3 Qxh3 8. e4 Nf6 9. exd5 Nxd5 *

