{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 6. Bb2. Black attacks the b3 structure and seeks open queenside lines. White must calculate the pawn contact before adding a routine knight move. The b2 bishop and a1 rook can become targets when files open. A queenside attack may matter even if your king plans to castle short. } 6. Bb2 a4 7. a3 axb3 8. cxb3 Bg4 *

