{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 6. Qxd8+. The exchanges open the d-file and allow White to remove queens. Black loses castling rights, but with queens gone the main issue is piece activity and pawn targets. Black's centralized king may become useful if the position simplifies further. A lost castling right alone does not prove an advantage. } 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 7. Ne2 Bf5 8. Nd2 Bc5 *

